    "created_at": "2016-01-07T06:53:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-07T06:53:55Z",
    "body": "Digging into the ES end of this a bit more, builtin functions have `[[ScriptOrModule]]` set to null, afaict.  See https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-createbuiltinfunction\n\nA bound function isn't even a Function object in terms of the ES spec, afaict.  It's created in https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-boundfunctioncreate and just has a special `[[Call]]`.  So it would not have a `[[ScriptOrModule]]` of its own.  Given that, calling `GetActiveScriptOrModule` inside that `postMessage` invocation seems like it would fail the assert in step 5.   This happens because https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-built-in-function-objects-call-thisargument-argumentslist will set the running execution context to the `calleeContext`, which gets `F`'s `[[ScriptOrModule]]`, which as noted above is null.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
